 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:15:20.679729Z",
 "text": "No, this clause is not enforceable. \n\nUnder **section 20(1)** of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a landlord is responsible for providing and maintaining a rental unit in a good state of repair, fit for habitation, and in compliance with health, safety, housing, and maintenance standards. Crucially, **section 20(2)** explicitly states that this obligation applies *even if the tenant was aware of a state of non-repair before entering into the tenancy agreement*. Because landlords and tenants cannot contract out of the Act (sections 3(1) and 4(1) render any inconsistent lease provision void), the tenant's acknowledgment and agreement to waive the repair is legally ineffective.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 20",
